00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.350 align:start position:0%
 
not everyone should code  you don't need to run a scientific study  to know that most people who tried to  learn coding failed miserably  all of these people have something in  common  which made them incapable of becoming  software developers  you will most probably suck in  programming if you have these signs  sign number one  you don't like sitting  if you don't like to spend unlimited  thousands of hours sitting at a desk in  front of a computer monitor all day  programming might not be for you  it's as simple as that  that's what software developers do sit  in front of a computer and develop  software  the basic job function requires you to  be in front of a keyboard writing code  the only good thing here is it's like  playing video games  once you start to enjoy it thousands of  hours of sitting will pass by relatively  quickly  nevertheless if you don't want to sit in  front of a computer you don't want to  become a software developer  sign number two  no interest in solving a puzzle  programming is more like solving puzzles  programming is a combination of your  knowledge of a particular language such  as python c or javascript and how well  you can apply it using your logical  ability  the primary puzzle every programmer has  to solve is to make a computer do a  particular task the world of programming  is very flexible  there are innumerable solutions to each  and every coding problem out there some  more efficient than others  therefore to be an effective software  developer one has to apply their brains  and find the most efficient solution  possible for every coding task at hand  if you do not enjoy this type of brain  intensive work  then you should definitely think if  software development is a right fit for  you  sign number three  no excitement after solving a problem  if you don't feel a sense of excitement  and accomplishment after solving a  problem  you will never be successful as a  programmer  you have to be excited about what you  have been doing and feeling drowsiness  by seeing those black lines in the  command prompt window  after solving a problem no matter if it  is hard or easy if you are not motivated  or excited then sorry programming  probably is not your thing  sign number four  you like repetitive tasks  programmers are really creative  they do not like being repetitive  taskers and if they find some part of  any repetitive task  they write a piece of software to  automate it  so if you prefer repetitive tasks less  mentally taxing that allow you to let  your mind wander and new tasks overwhelm  you in that sense  programming might not be a good place  for you  sign number five  low frustration tolerance  to build a project of significant scope  you have to be the type that isn't  easily defeated  in particular you can't become  frustrated while debugging and give up  on the project  not all smart people have this  personality trait  best computer programmers usually have a  high tolerance for failure  they often have to implement the same  algorithm many times before finding how  to do it correctly  and then after the perfect solution has  been found  they often realize that they need to  redo everything this is called  refactoring  when the program does something wrong  software developers view this as a  challenge rather than a frustration  besides consider this fact  programming takes a while to master and  if you're new to programming there are  many people better than you  if you're used to being the smartest in  the room this can be a humbling and  frustrating experience  sign number six  not a team player and full of ego  programmers try to minimize ego by  emphasizing that they code for the team  and with the team  it's not about you  it's about the team the code the client  the stakeholders and the customers  positive feedback and celebrating  success as a team is also essential  if you have a high ego it is usually  hard to ask for help or accept criticism  from others offering a better coding  solution  if you are not a team player you should  not consider programming as your career  sign number seven  if you want to be told what to do  every program is different  every algorithm is different  the programming landscape changes every  day  faster and faster  there will never be a situation where  someone will be able to tell you what to  do  they will tell you what they need and  you will have to figure out how to do it  on your own  over and over and over again  you sure can have a mentor initially but  in the long run you are on your own  sign number eight  zero patience  programming is like parenting  an idea is being provided or forced on  you  now you need to nurture it no matter how  hard or how complicated it is  you need to find a way to understand it  you want it to be perfect in every way  it can be  and to do that requires a lot of  patience  besides without patience  a person will not spend sufficient time  to study a coding problem and generate  the best possible solution  on top of that you have to love  debugging to be a programmer which  requires a lot of patience as well  to do it effectively you must remain  calm at least common enough to think  straight  if you can't focus your own thoughts on  coding problems with consistent patience  programming is most likely not a good  fit for you  sign number nine  aversion against googling  the programmers who have reached the  level of expertise in the field of  software development are very effective  at using google  stack overflow  github and other online resources to  build a technical knowledge advantage  anyone unwilling to use search engines  for at least an hour each day should not  consider a software developer job  sign number 10  if you have never said  there's got to be a better way  the best software programmers  continuously search for the better way  to accomplish their work  it is the very essence of computer  programming that we are always trying to  find ways to do everything better  if you are not curious enough to search  for a better way then programming is  definitely not for you  if you found this video useful i'd  appreciate it if you smash the like  button and click on the notification  bell  also make sure to subscribe to the  coding tech channel for more videos like  this in the future

